{"name":"Electric Indigo","hex":"#6600ff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"electric","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, produced by, operated with, or utilising electricity; electrical.","Of or relating to an electronic version of a musical instrument that has an acoustic equivalent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electricity; the electricity supply.","An electric powered version of something that was originally or is more commonly not electric.\n An electric car, locomotive, train etc.\n\nAn electric toothbrush.\n\nAn electric typewriter."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electric"},{"term":"indigo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A purplish-blue color.","A greenish dark blue color; the color of indigo dye."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["having a deep purplish-blue colour"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indigo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Indigo","blocks":[{"text":"Indigo is a term used for a number of hues in the region of blue. The word comes from the ancient dye of the same name. The term \"indigo\" can refer to the color of the dye, various colors of fabric dyed with indigo dye, a spectral color, one of the seven colors of the rainbow as described by Sir Isaac Newton, or a region on the color wheel, and can include various shades of blue, ultramarine, and green-blue. Since the web era, the term has also been used for various purple and violet hues identified as \"indigo\", based on use of the term \"indigo\" in HTML web page specifications."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Indian_indigo_dye_lump.jpg/330px-Indian_indigo_dye_lump.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigo"},{"title":"Electricity","blocks":[{"text":"Electricity is the set of physical phenomena associated with the presence and motion of matter possessing an electric charge. Electricity is related to magnetism, both being part of the phenomenon of electromagnetism, as described by Maxwell's equations. Common phenomena are related to electricity, including lightning, static electricity, electric heating, electric discharges and many others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/London_MMB_%C2%BB1E6_Lightning.jpg/330px-London_MMB_%C2%BB1E6_Lightning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electricity"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Passerina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg/500px-Passerina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Passerina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg/500px-Passerina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APasserina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Lactarius_indigo_%28Schwein.%29_Fr_939963.jpg/500px-Lactarius_indigo_%28Schwein.%29_Fr_939963.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Lactarius_indigo_%28Schwein.%29_Fr_939963.jpg/500px-Lactarius_indigo_%28Schwein.%29_Fr_939963.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALactarius_indigo_(Schwein.)_Fr_939963.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/1923ca_Quarter_anna_Bundi_indigo_SG26a_Mi18.jpg/500px-1923ca_Quarter_anna_Bundi_indigo_SG26a_Mi18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/1923ca_Quarter_